.TH QYPR-RECORD 1 "2026-07-11" "qypr-lock" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qypr-record \- notification mirror daemon for qypr-lock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qypr-record
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qypr-record
is a lightweight, standalone background service that mirrors the
.B org.freedesktop.Notifications
queue so that
.BR qypr-lock (1)
can display the backlog of undismissed notifications that arrived before the
screen was locked.
.PP
It runs as a separate binary from
.B qypr-lock
so that the heavy graphical and security dependencies (Wayland, Cairo, Pango,
PAM, mpv, ...) are not loaded into a long-lived background process, keeping its
idle memory footprint small. It observes notification traffic through a D-Bus
monitor connection (the same mechanism as
.BR "busctl monitor" )
and tracks dismissals, handing the queue to the lock screen over D-Bus at
startup (the
.B org.qypr.Notifications
interface).
.PP
The service is normally started via the provided systemd user unit
.IR qypr-notification-log.service .
.SH OPTIONS
None. The daemon takes no command-line arguments and runs until terminated.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Required for the session D-Bus connection.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Used to locate per-user state for the notification log.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/qypr-notification-log.service
The systemd user unit that launches
.BR qypr-record .
.SH SYSTEMD INTEGRATION
Install and enable the unit to carry the pre-lock notification backlog:
.PP
.RS
.nf
install -Dm644 systemd/qypr-notification-log.service \\
    ~/.config/systemd/user/qypr-notification-log.service
systemctl --user daemon-reload
systemctl --user enable --now qypr-notification-log.service
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The daemon shut down cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
Failed to start the D-Bus monitor or the notification log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qypr-lock (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR busctl (1),
.BR org.freedesktop.Notifications (5)
.SH AUTHORS
The qypr project.
